{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1110154-how-would-garou-law-punish-rape-committed-upon-metis-heavy-issue","id":1110154,"title":"How would Garou Law punish rape committed *upon* Metis? (Heavy Issue)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-01T07:34:18-07:00","id":1110154,"title":"How would Garou Law punish rape committed *upon* Metis? (Heavy Issue)","content":"&quot;Garou Shalt Not Mate With Garou&quot; was clawed/chiseled into the First Tablets of Litany to ultimately prevent the creation of Metis, convoluted philosophical justifications to condemn lovemaking <i>with</i> contraceptives between Garou notwithstanding.<br /> <br /> Now, herein lies the dilemma.<br /> <br /> War Rape amongst Garou <i>do</i> unfortunately happen (however rare), and unfortunate &quot;children of violence&quot; do frequently result. Naturally, the worthless beast responsible is given a jolly-good-castrating if they are allowed to <b>live</b> at all, with the poor mother STILL bearing the stigma of being a &quot;Charach&quot;<br /> <br /> But what if the victim in question is a Metis, from whom NO new distorted/disabled/disgraceful monster will EVER be born in spite of the rape, AND already being a second-class-citizen in Garou Society, on top of that?<br /> <br /> Naturally, The Black Furies would tear the brute apart and mail each piece to known rapists in the Garou nation as a warning. A Metis Sister is STILL a Sister.<br /> <br /> I would imagine however, that the alcoholic whoremongering-hypocrites of the Fianna would be MOST lenient in sentencing the rapist, ESPECIALLY if he too is Fianna. And if the <b>poor lass herself</b> is Fianna? Why, those child-abusing leprechauns would more than likely give the rapist a slap on the wrist and let bygones be bygones. After all, to them the Metis are not even living things, much less their proudly-trumpeted &quot;beloved family and kin&quot;, and what happened would likely be regarded as little worse the glorified masturbation. &quot;No Metis, No Fuss; have a pint of Guiness down at the pub with us Laddy, we all slip up sometimes.&quot; (SPITS in contempt)<br /> <br /> Sorry, had to get that off my chest: I REALLY <b>despise</b> trash who love to sleep around but are not willing to love, care for and raise the consequences of said sleeping around.<br /> <br /> Long sentence short:<br /> <br /> 1) Would rape committed against Metis, who themselves cannot bear distorted/disgraceful children, not be judged as harshly as a result in Garou Law?<br /> <br /> 2) The Metis herself would probably be treated/hounded/disgraced worse than her rapist, wouldn't she? Considering the already-disgraceful circumstances of her very <i>existence.</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 3) Or maybe, just maybe, would her family and kinfolk love her and defend her honor, even if the Litany Breaking committed against her would not result in what the Law was written to prevent?<br /> <br /> 4) How would the other 11 tribes handles this thorny dilemma?<br /> <br /> 5) Are there ANY such things as Fianna who would show respect and kindness to a Metis, for that matter?<br /> <br /> Sigh... the things you think about when you are morbidly depressed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 07-01-2017, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T09:05:24-07:00","id":1110209,"title":"","content":"I'd actually say no matter what tribe, rape would be treated as a VERY nope-thing even done to a metis.<br /> <br /> For one, it is an act of the Wyrm. Second, rape implies willingness to commit such acts out of a free will. Third, you got kinfolk, why the heck do you take pains to force another garou, a deformed garou at that, to sex? It implies the rapist has a LOT wrong about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T09:30:53-07:00","id":1110228,"title":"","content":"What is equally worrying is; would the reputation, feelings, dignity and &quot;humanity&quot; of the poor traumatized and emotionally-scarred Metis even <i>matter</i> in trials like this? Or will it become all be about the misconduct and disgrace of brute in question, as far as the &quot;proper&quot; Garou are concerned? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T13:26:50-07:00","id":1110326,"title":"","content":"Yes, it would matter because rape is of the Wyrm and the Metis is a Garou. You might as well ask if it is alright to kill and barbecue a Metis because it is the same level of sin to the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T13:57:58-07:00","id":1110344,"title":"","content":"I think such lessons are less an &quot;official&quot; issue than that it would lead to blood feuds between packs, septs, and tribes.<br /> <br /> However, I don't think rape occurs much between Garou. When the victim of such a crime can turn into Crinos and deal aggravated damage, that will scare away almost 100% of such criminals. Most crimes are crimes of opportunity, and criminals look for EASY targets. They look for people who are alone, vulnerable, or otherwise easy prey who will not or cannot resist. Even if the criminal believed he could defeat his target in combat, he'd know that he'd likely suffer some kind of aggravated damage, be identified, and would be an easy target for reprisals by the metis' family, pack, and possibly others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T14:08:54-07:00","id":1110347,"title":"","content":"Well, the Fianna are far from being my favorite tribe, but I can1t help but wonder, why the OP despises them so much, exactly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T15:35:04-07:00","id":1110393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1110154-how-would-garou-law-punish-rape-committed-upon-metis-heavy-issue#post1110154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Garou Shalt Not Mate With Garou&quot; was clawed/chiseled into the First Tablets of Litany to ultimately prevent the creation of Metis,...</div> </div> </div> </div>Was it? We don't know that. We know that the Litany says Garou aren't supposed to mate with Garou. The Litany doesn't say anything about Metis, which is why most Tribes don't approve of non-procreative sex between Garou at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1) Would rape committed against Metis, who themselves cannot bear distorted/disgraceful children, not be judged as harshly as a result in Garou Law? </div> </div> </div>No. Nothing in Garou Law suggests that the victim being a Metis would change anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) The Metis herself would probably be treated/hounded/disgraced worse than her rapist, wouldn't she? Considering the already-disgraceful circumstances of her very <i>existence.</i> </div> </div> </div>Nothing suggests this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Or maybe, just maybe, would her family and kinfolk love her and defend her honor, even if the Litany Breaking committed against her would not result in what the Law was written to prevent? </div> </div> </div>Most Metis have people that care about them, and would react to someone raping their family/friend/loved one/etc. with the same reaction the rest of us would.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) How would the other 11 tribes handles this thorny dilemma? </div> </div> </div>There is no dilemma. Rapists are bad, they get punished. The victims of rape are victims to be helped. None of the Tribes (even the Fianna) are presented as being so anti-Metis that raping a Metis would be acceptable in any circumstance.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T17:00:45-07:00","id":1110409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1110154-how-would-garou-law-punish-rape-committed-upon-metis-heavy-issue?p=1110347#post1110347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Fianna are far from being my favorite tribe, but I can1t help but wonder, why the OP despises them so much, exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, For a tribe that supposedly values &quot;Love for One's Family and Kin&quot; so much, they can awfully *flexible* in their values when it comes to Metis.<br /> <br /> And Garou or not, &quot;Respect All Beneath Ye, All Are of Gaia&quot; is a Noble and Kind Law; it should *Especially* apply to a helpless infant of your own flesh and blood, who should be Loved, Protecred and Cherished, not raised with hate and abuse, when they are not outright beaten to death with a stone minutes after birth to &quot;save face&quot;<br /> <br /> Not surprising then why so many Black Spiral Dancers have red hair and green eyes; better to be loved and accepted by &quot;monsters&quot; than to be bullied and hated by so-called &quot;heroes.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Hence why I'm not fond of the Fianna; and hence why I presumed they would be lenient towards injustice committed on Metis (even their own), as they have no love and respect for them in the first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 07-01-2017, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T17:56:42-07:00","id":1110420,"title":"","content":"Black Spiral Dancers can be of any ethnicity or race, so I do not see what your point is about red hair and green eyes. Most Celts do not have neither red hair or green eyes (blue eyes are more common than green eyes among Celtic populations) and the majority of people with red hair and green eyes have no Celtic blood. In fact, blue/green eyes occur in 56% of the Slovenes population and redhair occurs in the Udmurt people at almost the same level of the Irish. While the Fianna probably have a slightly higher occurrence of red hair and green eyes than any other Garou Tribe, any Tribe with European members will likely have a good proportion of red hair and green eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T21:07:00-07:00","id":1110458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1110154-how-would-garou-law-punish-rape-committed-upon-metis-heavy-issue?p=1110420#post1110420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Spiral Dancers can be of any ethnicity or race, so I do not see what your point is about red hair and green eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a paraphrase of a Fireside Conversation between concerning the Litany between Fianna Tribemates from <i>Tribebook: Fianna Revised</i>; a particularly angry and bitter metis basically sneered &quot;There are a LOT of Metis out there with Red Hair and Green eyes out there&quot; during the &quot;Garou Shalt Not Mate With Garou&quot; line of conversation. It was my sarcastic way of agreeing &quot;for a tribe that hates its metis, these Irishmen sure does love making them.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T23:19:31-07:00","id":1110481,"title":"","content":"I never did get why people think Metis are that common (I know that they are overrepresented in the books, but so are Lupus). I would think that most Garou see it as a form of incest taboo, so I doubt it would happen with any Garou who is capable of dealing with Kinfolk and Mortals (anyone with Rage 5-).<br /> <br /> When it comes to affairs of the heart, male Garou are particularly blessed. On average, they have dozens of female Kinfolk throwing themselves at them and they can awaken the primal sexuality within any responsive straight mortal woman, so they are only sleeping alone when they want to sleep alone. The last thing they should want to do is effectively sleep with their sisters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T08:47:59-07:00","id":1110558,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#800000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This thread appears to be, at it's core, an excuse to bag on the Irish framed around an already sensitive subject.<br /> <br /> I am locking it down, but thank you to everyone who attempted to make it an effective discussion.</span></b></span></span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\"> Forum Rules - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Onyx Path provides this forum as a gathering place for players and readers of our game